  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Il a été tiré de cet ouvrage pour le compte de Herman Daled, d'Yves Gevaert et de Paul Lebeer, 44 exemplaires sur papier d'épreuve protégés par une couverture en carton mince et une jaquette transparente, dont 4 marqués de A à D et 40 numérotés de 1 à 40, signés et datés par l'auteur"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Library has copy no. 34, signed and dated by the Broodthaers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cover title</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Reproduced in this artist's book is the title page of Baudelaire's Oeuvres completes, published  in the Bibliothèque de la Pléiade, Paris, 1971, including the leaf with the section title "Sur la Belgique"; the rest of the publication consists of blank leaves reproducing the original frame, the  the  running title "Pauvre Belgique" and the pagination 1318-1457. The places of publication are fictitious, the book was most likely published in Brussels, printed for Herman Daled, Yves Gevaert and Paul Lebeer, all three resident in Brussels.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes semi-opaque glassine jacket with the title ABCABCABCABCA obscuring the title "Pauvre Belgique" on the front cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Library's copy in red cloth folder housed in matching slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
